# API layer

`src/api/football_data.rs` wraps football-data.org; `src/api/espn.rs` wraps ESPN's public NFL endpoints. `ApiError` + rate-limit handling are shared in `src/api/mod.rs`.

**Belongs in `api/`:**
- Client methods that map 1:1 to endpoints (`FootballDataApi`, `EspnNflApi`)
- Serde structs matching API JSON (`Team`, `Match`, `SquadPlayer`, `Scorer`; `NflTeam`, `NflGame`) and the string→id plumbing ESPN needs
- Shared client construction (`FootballDataApi::from_env`, `EspnNflApi::new` with its required `User-Agent`)

**Belongs in domain modules (not `api/`):**
- `soccer.rs`: `fetch_squads_for_teams` (multi-call orchestration + role filter), `full_time_score`, team classification helpers
- `nfl/season.rs`: season-year rollover, scoreboard date range, `game_report` (completed + pool-eligible + scored), round titles
- `tiebreaker.rs`: `RosterPlayer`, `find_players` (sport-agnostic)

Team name lookup for registration uses `League::find_team` on `CatalogTeam`.

Soccer league modules construct the client with `FootballDataApi::from_env(data.http.clone())`; NFL uses `EspnNflApi::new(data.http.clone())`.
